messages:
Zoe Park: Heads-up I hit failures trying the Rust quickstart. curl example uses `REDWOOD_API_KEY` while the Rust snippet reads `std::env::var("REDWOOD_KEY")` -> 401 when you copy/paste.

Omar Khan: Yeah I saw that too. Also the README still imports `redwood_sdk` but the crate was renamed to `redwood_inference` in v0.9. Build fails on `cargo build`. Bad first-run experience.

Zoe Park: The Rust snippet also calls the client without tokio even though it uses async fn. We should show a blocking/compat example or the tokio attribute consistently.

Ria Desai: Reproduced locally. There's a manual retry loop around the request in the sample app that will replay POSTs on 5xx. The SDK now does safe retries for idempotent ops, so that wrapper can cause duplicate side effects. Recommend removing it and adding a short note about disabling SDK retries if you need custom behavior.

Omar Khan: Agreed. Proposed changes: switch env var to `REDWOOD_API_KEY` everywhere, update crate import to `redwood_inference = "^0.9"` in Cargo.toml example, remove manual retry wrapper, and add two Rust snippets: one sync/blocking using `tokio::runtime::Runtime::new().unwrap().block_on(...)` and one idiomatic async with `#[tokio::main] async fn main()`. Also add `Client::new(api_key).with_retries(0)` example for advanced users.

Zoe Park: Can you also add a tiny Cargo.toml snippet and a PowerShell example for setting env vars on Windows? New hires hit that all the time.

Omar Khan: Yep will include those. Draft Rust snippet I'll push:
```rust
use redwood_inference::Client;
use std::env;
#[tokio::main]
async fn main() {
    let api_key = env::var("REDWOOD_API_KEY").expect("set REDWOOD_API_KEY");
    let client = Client::new(&api_key);
    let resp = client.generate("Write a short limerick about latency").await.unwrap();
    println!("{}", resp.text);
}
```

Ria Desai: Nice. Also add a one-line callout about token scopes (generation vs embeddings) so folks don't paste the wrong key and get permission errors.

Omar Khan: PR opened: https://git.redwood/docs/pull/3321 — updates: env var parity to REDWOOD_API_KEY, crate rename, async/sync snippets, remove manual retry, Cargo.toml snippet, Windows env example, and token scope note. Requesting @ria review.

docs-bot: docs-bot: Added label `DX`, requested reviewers: @zia, @ria.

Ria Desai: Reviewed, left one nit on wording for the PowerShell snippet. Approved after tiny edit.

